1. Fixed the std::bad_weak_ptr crash (architectural fix)
Across all three nodes, shared_from_this() was being called inside the constructor — invalid in ROS 2, since the object isn't yet owned by a shared_ptr at that point. You split each node into an empty constructor + a separate init() method that does all the ROS-dependent setup, called from main() right after std::make_shared<Node>().

feature_tracker_node.cpp — constructor emptied, plus fixed a leftover nested function (a function defined inside another function, which isn't valid C++)
estimator_node.cpp (vins_estimator) — same split; had two shared_from_this() calls to move
pose_graph_node.cpp — checked, didn't actually need this fix, but you touched it for the next issue below

2. Fixed pose_graph's missing dependency (CMakeLists.txt)
Added find_package(ament_index_cpp REQUIRED) and included it in ament_target_dependencies(), plus an install(DIRECTORY ../support_files ...) rule so the loop-closure vocabulary file actually gets installed.
3. Fixed hardcoded/broken paths

euroc_config.yaml — output paths were hardcoded to a different developer's home directory (/home/prathana/...); corrected to your machine's path
Loop-closure vocabulary path in pose_graph — was using a leftover ROS 1-style relative path; replaced with ament_index_cpp::get_package_share_directory("pose_graph")

4. Fixed launch files (the bulk of your modified file count)

All the .launch / .launch.py files (3dm, black_box, cla, euroc, euroc_no_extrinsic_param, realsense_color, realsense_fisheye, tum, vins_rviz, vins_vicon_room1) — modernized ROS 1 XML syntax ($(find) → $(find-pkg-share)), fixed node execution tags and data types for ROS 2
Specifically added the missing config_file parameter to pose_graph's launch entry — it was being passed to the other two nodes but not this one, which is why pose_graph kept crashing even after the config fix

